div.head:
TO THE RIGHT HONOURABLE THOMAS,
EARL OF DANBY, VISCOUNT LATIMER, AND BARON OSBORNE OF KIVETON IN YORKSHIRE;
LORD HIGH TREASURER OF ENGLAND, ONE OF HIS MAJESTY'S MOST HONOURABLE PRIVY COUNCIL, AND KNIGHT OF THE MOST NOBLE ORDER OF THE GARTER[1].

cell.p:
Dola. O, she has touched him in the tenderest part;
See how he reddens with despite and shame,
To be out-done in generosity!
